        - 'citation': If this is a case, use One Bluebook form official citation for the case, It should include (court year) or (year) in parentheses.  If this item is code / statutes / rules  when germane.  Include statutes/rules when germane (e.g., Fed. R. Civ. P. 9(b); 15 U.S.C. § 1125(c)).
        Here are some general rules about Bluebook formatted citations:
        a. Full case citation format **without pincite**: Case Name, Volume Reporter Page (Court Year).
        b. Omit the court name only if the reporter uniquely identifies the court, e.g.: 
        U.S. (U.S. Supreme Court) → use (Year) only. Year is the year of decision.
        State official reporters for the state's highest court (e.g., Cal. 4th, N.Y.3d) → use (Year) only.
        Otherwise, include court and year in parentheses. Year is the year of decision.
        - 'parenthetical': a short parenthetical explaining the key legal proposition and how it applies here, or a brief quote or paraphrase from the authority to illustrate relevance. always wrap the content in parenthesis. 
   
